  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  @  CauchQ
  @  Quantile: the X below which the probability is p.
  @  Author & design          : Jean Wilson
  @  Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  @  Arguments may be given loose or bundled in a list of 3; that list is
  @  what LastArguments reports, and its length is checked before use.
  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  IF DUP TypeName "list" == THEN IF DUP Size 3 ≠ THEN "CauchQ: needs 3 arguments" DoError END Explode Drop END
  → x0v scv pv « x0v 0 + scv 0 + pv 0 + → x0 sc p « 'x0-sc*1000000000000' →Num 'x0+sc*1000000000000' →Num 0 0 → lo hi x d « 1 80 START '(lo+hi)/2' →Num 'x' STO '(0.5+2*UVAL(UBASE(ATAN((x-x0)/sc))))' →Num 'd' STO 'IFTE(d<p;x;lo)' →Num 'lo' STO 'IFTE(d<p;hi;x)' →Num 'hi' STO NEXT '(lo+hi)/2' →Num 'x' STO 1 2 START 'IFTE(ABS(1/(Ⓒπ*sc*(1+((x-x0)/sc)^2)))>0.000000000000000000000000000001;x-((0.5+2*UVAL(UBASE(ATAN((x-x0)/sc))))-p)/(1/(Ⓒπ*sc*(1+((x-x0)/sc)^2)));x)' →Num 'd' STO 'IFTE((d>lo) AND (d<hi);d;x)' →Num 'x' STO NEXT x x0v scv pv 3 →List Drop » » »
